WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.404 --> 00:00:02.759
- In life, it's a very simple principle,

00:00:02.759 --> 00:00:05.988
but all success comes
from completing tasks.

00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:09.477
Fully functioning people, these
are the top 10% of people,

00:00:09.477 --> 00:00:11.580
never complain and never explain.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.353
If you're stuck in a dead
end job that you can't leave,

00:00:14.353 --> 00:00:16.410
because you have no money set aside,

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.174
you have put a brake on your potential.

00:00:19.174 --> 00:00:21.218
- Hello, Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:21.218 --> 00:00:24.505
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:24.505 --> 00:00:27.674
are going to solve all of the
major problems of the world.

00:00:27.674 --> 00:00:28.905
So, to help you on your journey,

00:00:28.905 --> 00:00:31.208
today we're going to learn
from motivational speaker,

00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:33.852
author and sales expert Brian Tracy

00:00:33.852 --> 00:00:37.435
and my take on his Top 10
Rules for Success, Volume Two.

00:00:37.435 --> 00:00:39.155
Rule number two is my personal favorite,

00:00:39.155 --> 00:00:41.618
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:41.618 --> 00:00:43.292
And as always, guys, as you're watching,

00:00:43.292 --> 00:00:45.653
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:45.653 --> 00:00:47.419
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:47.419 --> 00:00:49.865
put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired,

00:00:49.865 --> 00:00:52.331
and when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:52.331 --> 00:00:54.893
to stick for yourself as well.

00:00:54.893 --> 00:00:55.726
Enjoy.

00:00:58.706 --> 00:01:01.456
(dramatic music)

00:01:08.822 --> 00:01:12.819
- Act as if you already
had a goal that you desire.

00:01:12.819 --> 00:01:14.467
So, let us say, for example, that you

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.302
want to be financially independent.

00:01:16.302 --> 00:01:18.356
You want to be financially successful.

00:01:18.356 --> 00:01:21.044
How would you behave if you
were financially successful?

00:01:21.044 --> 00:01:23.659
How would you dress, how
would you organize your life?

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:25.510
How would you treat other people?

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.240
Sometimes I say, imagine that you

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.128
are financially independent.

00:01:29.128 --> 00:01:30.813
You're independently wealthy,

00:01:30.813 --> 00:01:34.190
and you're only doing your
current job as a curtesy

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.561
to your boss and to keep
yourself busy during the day,

00:01:37.561 --> 00:01:39.872
but basically you're an
extremely wealthy person.

00:01:39.872 --> 00:01:41.222
You've inherited an enormous

00:01:41.222 --> 00:01:43.666
amount of money from some source.

00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:45.862
How would you behave if you were already

00:01:45.862 --> 00:01:49.194
the wealthy person that you desire to be?

00:01:49.194 --> 00:01:51.525
Many people don't realize that,

00:01:51.525 --> 00:01:55.012
if you behave like a poor person,
there's an old saying that

00:01:55.012 --> 00:01:57.684
poor people, poor folks have poor ways.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:00.553
If you behave like a poor
person, you'll always be poor.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:05.175
If you dress like a bum,
if you have a messy home

00:02:05.175 --> 00:02:07.924
or apartment, if your car is dirty

00:02:07.924 --> 00:02:11.115
with junk in the back seat,
that's how poor people live.

00:02:11.115 --> 00:02:13.518
And, what happens is that
you're surrounding yourself

00:02:13.518 --> 00:02:15.258
with the image of being poor,

00:02:15.258 --> 00:02:17.548
and you cannot change your outer world

00:02:17.548 --> 00:02:20.074
until you change your inner world.

00:02:20.074 --> 00:02:21.832
Ask yourself what are the three

00:02:21.832 --> 00:02:25.142
most important things
that I do in my work?

00:02:25.142 --> 00:02:28.465
And, then you have to discipline yourself

00:02:28.465 --> 00:02:32.059
to start with the most important task

00:02:32.059 --> 00:02:35.387
and work on that task
until it is completed.

00:02:35.387 --> 00:02:37.364
And, it's a very simple principle,

00:02:37.364 --> 00:02:39.811
but it is the beginning and the middle

00:02:39.811 --> 00:02:42.123
and the end of success.

00:02:42.123 --> 00:02:44.392
Decide on your most important task,

00:02:44.392 --> 00:02:47.908
begin immediately and work on that task

00:02:47.908 --> 00:02:52.261
with self discipline
until it is 100% complete.

00:02:52.261 --> 00:02:54.607
In life, it's a very simple principle,

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:58.714
but all success comes
from completing tasks.

00:02:58.714 --> 00:03:03.192
It's not from working at tasks,
it's from completing tasks.

00:03:03.192 --> 00:03:07.274
It is only when you complete
tasks that you are successful.

00:03:07.274 --> 00:03:11.471
The most important key
to success is to start

00:03:11.471 --> 00:03:15.638
and complete one important task
first thing in the morning.

00:03:17.511 --> 00:03:18.611
If you--

00:03:18.611 --> 00:03:19.444
- [Man] Eat the frog.

00:03:19.444 --> 00:03:20.408
- Eat the frog.

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:23.629
If you try to do many things,
you end up doing nothing.

00:03:23.629 --> 00:03:27.554
So, you make a list of all
your work before you begin,

00:03:27.554 --> 00:03:30.694
and then you ask, "If I
could only do on thing

00:03:30.694 --> 00:03:34.665
"on this list, which one
activity is the most important?"

00:03:34.665 --> 00:03:36.311
And then you do that activity,

00:03:36.311 --> 00:03:38.335
only that until it's complete.

00:03:38.335 --> 00:03:41.438
If you start every day
by completing a task,

00:03:41.438 --> 00:03:43.854
you will double and
triple your productivity.

00:03:43.854 --> 00:03:46.316
You will find that every
major change in your life

00:03:46.316 --> 00:03:48.762
is accompanied by a person or persons

00:03:48.762 --> 00:03:52.364
who either opens or closes doors for you.

00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:56.063
The possibility of your
achieving the best life for you

00:03:56.063 --> 00:03:58.000
will be determined by the number of people

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.167
who know you and like you and
who are willing to help you.

00:04:03.873 --> 00:04:06.977
Now, in order to broaden
your network of contacts,

00:04:06.977 --> 00:04:11.039
you must network continually
at every opportunity.

00:04:11.039 --> 00:04:12.804
There seems to be a direct relationship

00:04:12.804 --> 00:04:14.932
between the number of people you know

00:04:14.932 --> 00:04:17.181
and how successful you are.

00:04:17.181 --> 00:04:21.129
Now, to network successfully,
the simple strategy is this.

00:04:21.129 --> 00:04:24.495
When you meet a new person,
ask them what they do.

00:04:24.495 --> 00:04:26.171
Ask for their business card

00:04:26.171 --> 00:04:28.228
and then see if you can't find

00:04:28.228 --> 00:04:30.465
something that you can do for them.

00:04:30.465 --> 00:04:32.400
And, the one thing that
people like the most

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.359
is if you can send them a customer.

00:04:35.359 --> 00:04:36.942
Many people who network are thinking

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:39.193
"What can I get from this other person?"

00:04:39.193 --> 00:04:41.493
Your strategy when you meet a new person

00:04:41.493 --> 00:04:43.495
who can be helpful to you is to think

00:04:43.495 --> 00:04:45.383
"What can I give to this person?

00:04:45.383 --> 00:04:48.929
"What can do for this person
and how quickly can I do it?"

00:04:48.929 --> 00:04:51.656
That way, you sow seeds of people who'll

00:04:51.656 --> 00:04:54.120
be prepared to help you in the future.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.214
A fear of rejection is
caused by a hyper concern

00:04:57.214 --> 00:05:00.514
for the opinions of other people.

00:05:00.514 --> 00:05:03.178
In William Glasser's
work on what they call

00:05:03.178 --> 00:05:06.178
the fully functioning person,
they had a wonderful line.

00:05:06.178 --> 00:05:07.803
They said fully functioning people,

00:05:07.803 --> 00:05:10.030
these are the top 10% of people,

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.490
never complain and never explain.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.330
They never defend themselves,

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.121
is they do it or they don't do it,

00:05:16.121 --> 00:05:17.434
but they never feel that they have to

00:05:17.434 --> 00:05:19.705
explain themselves to anyone else.

00:05:19.705 --> 00:05:23.042
If someone doesn't like it,
they say, "And your point is?"

00:05:23.042 --> 00:05:25.805
And they just don't care.

00:05:25.805 --> 00:05:27.475
And, your job is to reach the point

00:05:27.475 --> 00:05:29.305
where you say "I like myself.

00:05:29.305 --> 00:05:30.181
"I like myself.

00:05:30.181 --> 00:05:32.389
"I'm responsible for own life,

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:35.192
"and if someone doesn't
like what I do or don't do,

00:05:35.192 --> 00:05:37.603
"that's their problem,
it's not my problem."

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:40.318
And if you repeat this to
yourself over and over again,

00:05:40.318 --> 00:05:42.410
you can actually reprogram yourself

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:47.130
and cancel out and override
all the previous programming

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.298
that's generating these fears that

00:05:49.298 --> 00:05:51.766
you experience in your adult life.

00:05:51.766 --> 00:05:54.121
Here's a very important story.

00:05:54.121 --> 00:05:57.104
They studied the 500 owners of

00:05:57.104 --> 00:05:59.753
the fastest growing
businesses in the world,

00:05:59.753 --> 00:06:03.257
and they asked them, "Why did
you choose this business?"

00:06:03.257 --> 00:06:05.583
And all of them said,
"I choose this business

00:06:05.583 --> 00:06:08.591
"because I really love the product.

00:06:08.591 --> 00:06:11.262
"I wanted the product for myself,

00:06:11.262 --> 00:06:14.476
"and, so, I developed it for myself."

00:06:14.476 --> 00:06:16.816
Like the founder of eBay was lookin'

00:06:16.816 --> 00:06:20.036
for a way to sell his candy dispensers.

00:06:20.036 --> 00:06:21.478
He had a collection.

00:06:21.478 --> 00:06:23.924
And there wasn't anything, so he created

00:06:23.924 --> 00:06:27.773
a little auction site on the
internet at the beginning,

00:06:27.773 --> 00:06:32.266
and then, he found he could
sell other things in an auction,

00:06:32.266 --> 00:06:33.596
and built eBay, one of the most

00:06:33.596 --> 00:06:35.417
successful companies in the world.

00:06:35.417 --> 00:06:39.012
But, he started it because
he wanted it for himself.

00:06:39.012 --> 00:06:41.715
So, you'll always be successful

00:06:41.715 --> 00:06:43.610
if you create the product or service

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.501
'cause it's something that you want

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:47.462
and believe in for yourself.

00:06:47.462 --> 00:06:50.481
Financial freedom means that
you're making enough money

00:06:50.481 --> 00:06:52.981
so that you don't have to
think about it continually,

00:06:52.981 --> 00:06:56.919
or, best of all, that you
never think about it at all.

00:06:56.919 --> 00:06:59.493
Most people worry about
money all the time,

00:06:59.493 --> 00:07:02.677
and that's a lousy way to live.

00:07:02.677 --> 00:07:04.915
Nearly 80% of the population is

00:07:04.915 --> 00:07:06.659
preoccupied with money problems.

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:08.158
They think about it when they wake up

00:07:08.158 --> 00:07:09.869
and they think about it during the day

00:07:09.869 --> 00:07:11.618
and they think about it when
they go to sleep at night

00:07:11.618 --> 00:07:14.893
and sometimes, it keeps
'em awake at night.

00:07:14.893 --> 00:07:18.109
The only way for you to
achieve financial freedom

00:07:18.109 --> 00:07:21.756
is for you to define your
financial goals clearly

00:07:21.756 --> 00:07:25.728
and then make plans to
achieve those goals.

00:07:25.728 --> 00:07:26.949
There is a process that
you've heard about,

00:07:26.949 --> 00:07:28.630
it's called serendipity.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.255
And, serendipity is defined as the process

00:07:31.255 --> 00:07:35.149
of making happy discoveries,
is that you find things

00:07:35.149 --> 00:07:37.640
that seem to conspire together

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.517
to bring you the things you want in life.

00:07:39.517 --> 00:07:42.099
You meet the right person,
you read the right article,

00:07:42.099 --> 00:07:44.435
you get the right email
or phone call and so on.

00:07:44.435 --> 00:07:46.969
It's called serendipity,
happy discoveries.

00:07:46.969 --> 00:07:48.636
Now, what they've found, and, by the way,

00:07:48.636 --> 00:07:51.863
this is a common factor
that you can tap into,

00:07:51.863 --> 00:07:55.675
what they found is that
people who are, seem to have

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:59.398
serendipitous, wonderfully
coincidental experiences,

00:07:59.398 --> 00:08:01.183
are people that are
characterized by one thing.

00:08:01.183 --> 00:08:02.898
They're looking.

00:08:02.898 --> 00:08:04.754
Nobody has a serendipitous experience

00:08:04.754 --> 00:08:06.813
sitting there watchin'
television at night,

00:08:06.813 --> 00:08:08.824
or reading the paper
or drinking in the bar.

00:08:08.824 --> 00:08:11.801
In other words, these
people who have these happy,

00:08:11.801 --> 00:08:13.113
just make these happy discoveries

00:08:13.113 --> 00:08:14.966
are people who are looking.

00:08:14.966 --> 00:08:17.584
And so, one of the most important
requirements for success,

00:08:17.584 --> 00:08:19.733
again, based on years
and years of research

00:08:19.733 --> 00:08:21.777
which I've done, is ambition.

00:08:21.777 --> 00:08:24.941
Ambition means that you're
hungry, is that you're hungry,

00:08:24.941 --> 00:08:27.288
you want to be successful.

00:08:27.288 --> 00:08:31.666
You want to be successful more
that almost anything else.

00:08:31.666 --> 00:08:36.653
Always choose higher quality
rather than lower cost.

00:08:36.653 --> 00:08:39.194
Most companies think the way to sell more

00:08:39.194 --> 00:08:41.045
is to lower the price.

00:08:41.045 --> 00:08:43.326
But, the true reason for success,

00:08:43.326 --> 00:08:45.460
and there's years of research,

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.461
is to improve the quality of your product.

00:08:48.461 --> 00:08:50.998
You improve the quality of your product.

00:08:50.998 --> 00:08:54.570
There was a study of the 500
fastest growing companies

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.962
in the world that came out last year.

00:08:56.962 --> 00:09:01.491
And, they found the number
one place where they invested

00:09:01.491 --> 00:09:04.319
was improving the quality of the product.

00:09:04.319 --> 00:09:06.795
That, if you had a certain amount of money

00:09:06.795 --> 00:09:10.651
to invest in your business,
it was not on advertising

00:09:10.651 --> 00:09:13.572
or machinery or computers.

00:09:13.572 --> 00:09:14.405
- Quality.

00:09:14.405 --> 00:09:15.651
- Improve the quality.

00:09:15.651 --> 00:09:17.056
That's the key to success.
- So.

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:19.946
- Having money in the bank
gives you greater freedom

00:09:19.946 --> 00:09:21.469
and the ability to take advantage

00:09:21.469 --> 00:09:24.143
of opportunities when they come along.

00:09:24.143 --> 00:09:26.347
If you're broke or in debt,

00:09:26.347 --> 00:09:28.188
and an opportunity comes along,

00:09:28.188 --> 00:09:29.966
you have no options open to you.

00:09:29.966 --> 00:09:31.589
There's nothing that you can do.

00:09:31.589 --> 00:09:34.256
So, having money makes you free.

00:09:36.239 --> 00:09:38.652
One of the most important
things I ever learned in life

00:09:38.652 --> 00:09:41.902
is that you're only as
free as your options.

00:09:41.902 --> 00:09:44.488
If you have no options, if you have to do

00:09:44.488 --> 00:09:46.159
whatever it is you're
doing, you have no choice,

00:09:46.159 --> 00:09:47.649
you have no freedom.

00:09:47.649 --> 00:09:50.565
If you're stuck in a dead
end job that you can't leave

00:09:50.565 --> 00:09:52.532
because you have no money set aside,

00:09:52.532 --> 00:09:55.124
you have put a brake on your potential.

00:09:55.124 --> 00:09:57.375
You are locked in place and you have

00:09:57.375 --> 00:09:59.389
no option for moving forward.

00:09:59.389 --> 00:10:01.252
You can end up spinning your wheels

00:10:01.252 --> 00:10:04.332
and losing months and years of your time

00:10:04.332 --> 00:10:06.994
by the very fact that you have no choice

00:10:06.994 --> 00:10:09.908
but to accept whatever
is being handed to you.

00:10:09.908 --> 00:10:13.350
But, if you have money, they
call this opportunity money,

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:14.884
if you have money put aside,

00:10:14.884 --> 00:10:17.467
you can walk away from a bad job

00:10:17.467 --> 00:10:21.669
and you can take time to find
exactly the right job for you.

00:10:21.669 --> 00:10:24.896
This idea of saving up
money so that you are

00:10:24.896 --> 00:10:27.062
available to take opportunities

00:10:27.062 --> 00:10:29.683
has transformed many people's lives.

00:10:29.683 --> 00:10:32.505
Let me leave you with the
last verse of Carry On.

00:10:32.505 --> 00:10:35.865
There are some who drift
out in the deserts of doubt,

00:10:35.865 --> 00:10:39.224
and some who in negativity wallow.

00:10:39.224 --> 00:10:41.047
There are others I know who in piety go

00:10:41.047 --> 00:10:43.165
because of a heaven to follow.

00:10:43.165 --> 00:10:46.754
But, to labor with zest
and to give of your best

00:10:46.754 --> 00:10:49.447
for the sweetness and joy of the giving,

00:10:49.447 --> 00:10:52.322
to help folks along
with a hand and a song,

00:10:52.322 --> 00:10:55.136
why there's the real sunshine of living.

00:10:55.136 --> 00:10:57.932
Carry on, carry on, fight
the good fight and true.

00:10:57.932 --> 00:10:59.466
There's big work to do.

00:10:59.466 --> 00:11:02.088
Believe in your mission,
greet life with a cheer,

00:11:02.088 --> 00:11:04.556
there's big work to do,
and that's why you're here.

00:11:04.556 --> 00:11:07.485
Carry on, carry on, that the
world be the better for you

00:11:07.485 --> 00:11:10.559
so, at last when you die,
let this be your cry,

00:11:10.559 --> 00:11:13.635
carry on, my soul, carry on.

00:11:13.635 --> 00:11:15.255
(clapping)
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:11:15.255 --> 00:11:17.005
ladies and gentlemen,

00:11:20.444 --> 00:11:24.611
if you will resolve with whatever
life hands you to carry on

00:11:25.565 --> 00:11:27.944
there is nothing that can stop you

00:11:27.944 --> 00:11:31.728
from achieving the greatness
for which you were created.

00:11:31.728 --> 00:11:32.561
Thank you.
- Hear!

00:11:32.561 --> 00:11:35.811
- God bless.
(clapping)

